# Accepted Trivy findings (ADR-008, ADD §6.2). A Critical or High finding blocks a release unless it is listed
# here with a reason and a date to look at it again — the same rule as ZAP false positives (ADR-020).
#
# Format: one vulnerability id per line, preceded by a comment:
#   # <reason> — review by YYYY-MM-DD
#   CVE-2026-12345

# go-jose v3 in the edge image's Caddy, no fixed version: DoS through crafted RSA parameters in a JWK. Caddy pulls it
# in only through smallstep/certificates, its internal CA and ACME server, which configs_production does not enable
# (no acme_server, pki or tls internal). Drop once a fix exists — review by 2027-01-11
CVE-2026-116587
